# 2026-08-26: FIXED by the template-clone isolation change (ADR-005) —
# a hole now belongs to its nearest enclosing generator, so wrapping
# the generator in close() no longer exposes the template's `_` to the
# overlay statement.  Historically (README, gap 5) this document
# absorbed `deploy: prod: x: 2` into the TEMPLATE: every environment
# grew a bogus `prod:` child carrying the overlay, the real prod.x
# stayed 1, and the run still EXITED 0.  Now the overlay merges with
# the generated prod child exactly as it does without close():
# dev {p:false,x:1}, prod {p:true,x:2}.  check.sh pins the CORRECT
# output against the golden; the shared spec pins it in both engines
# (test/spec/gen-close.tsv, close-pack-hole-overlay-merges).
environments: hide({ dev: { p: false }, prod: { p: true } })
deploy: close(pack($.environments, _ & { x: ***1 | integer }))
deploy: prod: x: 2
